# Commit message convention

This repository follows [Conventional Commits](https://www.conventionalcommits.org/).
Every commit message subject MUST match:

```
type(scope): description
```

## Rules

- `type` MUST be one of: `feat`, `fix`, `docs`, `style`, `refactor`, `perf`, `test`, `build`, `ci`, `chore`.
- `scope` is optional, wrapped in parentheses, and lowercase (e.g. `ci`, `build`, `deps`, `home`, `markdown`).
- `description`:
  - lowercase first letter,
  - imperative mood ("add", "fix", "refine", not "added"/"adds"),
  - no trailing period,
  - concise (aim for ≤ 72 characters).
- Do NOT append the PR number (e.g. `(#12)`) — GitHub adds it automatically on squash-merge.
- Add a blank line and a body only when extra context is genuinely useful.
- Keep one logical change per commit.

## Examples (from this repo's history)

- `feat: mobile adaptation`
- `feat(home): implement main page layout and styling`
- `fix: amend path of image url`
- `fix(build): recover params to fit the requirement of nextra`
- `chore(ci): change fixed path to github variables`
- `docs: add CONTRIBUTING.md`
